// ── Platform primitives (from "terse-sdk") ────────────────────
//
// Everything below ships with the terse-sdk package. This summary is the
// reference for job code — do not read the terse-sdk dist to rediscover it.
//
// Defining jobs:
//   createJob({ name, triggers: [...], states?, filter?, onTrigger, durable? })
//     Registers a workflow. `filter` and `onTrigger` receive (event, state);
//     `filter` returns boolean to decide whether the run proceeds.
//   Every trigger event has event.formatForAgentRunner(): string — the
//     canonical way to inline the triggering event into an agent prompt.
//
// Agentic execution:
//   generateText({ prompt, skills: [...], toolApprovals?, outputSchema? })
//     One-shot agent run. Returns Promise<string>, or Promise<z.infer<schema>>
//     when `outputSchema` (a zod schema) is given. Skills come from the
//     generated `Skills` export below; the agent can only touch integrations
//     whose skills are passed.
//   TerseAgent.create({ prompt, skills, toolApprovals? })
//     Streaming variant: `for await (const result of agent.run(message))`.
//     `agent.tools` is typed to the generated tools of the passed skills.
//
// Per-job state (typed key/value store):
//   states: [{ key: "runCount", value: z.number().default(0) }]
//   then `await state.get("runCount")` / `await state.set("runCount", n)`
//   in `filter`/`onTrigger`. Keys and value types come from the declaration.
//
// Durability (all of these require `durable: true` on the job):
//   step(client.method(args))   Journals a single wrapped call; arguments and
//                               result must be serializable.
//   jobStep({ run, input?, inputSchema?, outputSchema? })
//                               Journals a code block as one step.
//   sleep("2h" | ms | Date)     Suspends the run; resumes after the duration.
//   await log(...args)          Replay-safe console.log (prints exactly once).
//   waitForInput({ via: slack({ channel: SlackChannel.X.channelId }), prompt, options })
//                               Suspends until a human answers; resolves to
//                               { choice, text?, respondent }. `options` is
//                               [{ id, label, description?, freeText? }].
//
// Secrets:
//   Write with `terse secrets add`; read in job code via process.env.MY_SECRET.
//   There is no value-returning secrets API — env vars are the read side.
